==Description==
The '''Korblox Guard''' was an enemy that appeared in [[The Hunt: Mega Edition Event]]. It also appears in [[The Classic Event]] missions as part of [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode. It has higher health and faster speed than the [[Korblox Seeker (The Hunt: Mega Edition)|Korblox Seeker]]. On some waves, it could spawn with [[Bloated]] or [[Nimble]].

==Logbook Description==
"''Exiled by Knight Zargus to the frozen wastelands of The North, these barbarians perished after running out of supplies and refusing to eat the local rocks and crystals. The harsh climate preserved their bodies until defectors from Canavus' army formed the Necroborn tribe. There, their mysterious leader raised the fallen barbarians from death, transforming them into Korblox Guards.''"

==Appearance==
The '''Korblox Guard''' has blue skin. It wears a black shirt and pants, a blue helmet with grey outlines and blue neon spikes, and a red belt with a grey buckle. It wears an arm-pad and a knee-pad on its right arm and leg. There are also blue neon spikes on its right arm and leg. It does not have a left arm and leg, exposing its skeleton.

==Event Strategy==
As this enemy only appears through [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode, no strategy section is made for its current version. Instead, a strategy section for the one that appeared without [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode in [[Korblox Temple]] is listed instead.
*Because of its low health and high amount of cash obtained in the map, multiple early game towers like the [[Militant]], [[Mortar]], [[Medic]], [[Electroshocker]] and [[Brawler]] can be used to deal with this.
*As [[Korblox Temple]] gives a lot of cash per wave, high DPS towers like the [[Turret]], [[Accelerator]], [[Pursuit]] or [[Golden Minigunner]] can easily be afforded to deal with this, though this is not necessary as early-game towers on their own can deal with them just fine.

